MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. Nav drawer folder tree (AdapterNavAccountFolder): folders now render as a
   name-based hierarchy — indented per level, chevron on folders that have
   nav-visible children, tap chevron (or a non-selectable group row) to
   collapse/expand. State persists in folder.collapsed (existing column +
   DAO setter). Separator defaults to '/' for local (RSS) folders that have
   none; IMAP subfolders use their server separator, so mail accounts get
   the tree too. Subtrees under a collapsed ancestor are filtered in set().
2. Query: liveAccountFolder now carries folder.selectable + folder.collapsed
   (NULL placeholders on the account half of the UNION).
3. RSS drawer flood fix: group folders are now nav-drawer containers created
   navigation=true + collapsed=true, so a provisioned channel tree shows as
   a few collapsed groups instead of every channel flat. One-shot 0062
   migration in ensureFeedTree (pref comms_nav_tree_0062) upgrades existing
   installs' group folders the same way.
4. Respect per-channel choices: the 0056 'parity upgrade' in repairRssAccount
   forced notify/navigation back on for every feed folder on EVERY app start,
   silently undoing the user's per-channel hide/mute selections. Removed —
   defaults are set at folder creation only; 'show in navigation menu' in the
   folder list is now the authoritative per-channel selector.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
